    {
      "title": "Middleware Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Middleware Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Wraps the Whole App",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sees ==every request== before routing and ==every response== after the endpoint",
                "Fits cross-cutting work: **logging**, **timing**, **headers**, **auth checks**",
                "Code before `call_next` runs {green:on the way in}; code after runs {orange:on the way out}",
                "The ==first== middleware added is the **innermost** layer"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Last added",
                    "sub": "outermost",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "First added",
                    "sub": "innermost",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Endpoint",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Simplest Form",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@app.middleware('http')` uses ==BaseHTTPMiddleware== underneath",
                "Await `call_next`, then **return** its response"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.middleware('http')",
                "async def mw(request, call_next):",
                "    # in: before the endpoint",
                "    response = await call_next(request)",
                "    # out: after the endpoint",
                "    return response"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Middleware",
                "Dependency",
                "Route handler"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "**global**",
                  "per-route",
                  "one route"
                ],
                [
                  "Sees",
                  "raw request",
                  "parsed params",
                  "parsed params"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Forgot to return}: must return what `call_next` gave, or the request fails",
                "{red:Reading} ==await request.body()== in BaseHTTPMiddleware buffers it in memory; older Starlette broke the endpoint"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pure ASGI Middleware",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pure ASGI Middleware",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The ASGI Contract",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "App signature: ==async def `__call__(self, scope, receive, send)`==",
                "Middleware = class holding `self.app`, delegating with `await self.app(scope, receive, send)`",
                "`scope['type']` is {blue:http}, {purple:websocket} or {orange:lifespan}",
                "Always pass non-http scopes straight through"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class AddHeader:",
                "  def __init__(self, app, value): self.app, self.value = app, value",
                "  async def __call__(self, scope, receive, send):",
                "    if scope['type'] != 'http': return await self.app(scope, receive, send)",
                "    async def send_wrapper(message):",
                "      if message['type'] == 'http.response.start': message['headers'].append((b'x-app', self.value))",
                "      await send(message)",
                "    await self.app(scope, receive, send_wrapper)"
              ],
              "note": "wrap send to edit the response"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Wrapping send and Registering",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Intercept ==http.response.start== to edit headers, then forward",
                "`message['headers']` is a list of **byte-tuple** pairs",
                "Register: `add_middleware(Cls, option=value)`; kwargs go to `__init__(self, app, option)`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "app.add_middleware(AddHeader, value=b'v1')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pure ASGI vs BaseHTTPMiddleware",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Pure ASGI",
                "BaseHTTPMiddleware"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Extra task per request",
                  "{green:None}",
                  "{red:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Websockets, streaming",
                  "{green:Correct}",
                  "Pitfalls"
                ],
                [
                  "Contextvars, background tasks",
                  "{green:Safe}",
                  "Pitfalls"
                ],
                [
                  "Boilerplate",
                  "More",
                  "Less"
                ],
                [
                  "Request object",
                  "Build `Request(scope, receive)`",
                  "Given"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot the passthrough?",
              "text": "Without the ==http== check, websocket and lifespan scopes hit your http-only code and break."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Middleware Ordering",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Middleware Ordering",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stack Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Last== `add_middleware` call = **outermost** layer: first to see the request, last to see the response",
                "==First== one added sits closest to the app",
                "Request order is the **reverse** of registration; response order is registration order",
                "Register A then B: request path {blue:B → A → app}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Where Each Layer Goes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Layer",
                "Registered",
                "Order a request meets it (outermost first)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "TrustedHost",
                  "5th (last)",
                  "1"
                ],
                [
                  "CORS",
                  "4th",
                  "2"
                ],
                [
                  "GZip",
                  "3rd",
                  "3"
                ],
                [
                  "Request-ID / logging",
                  "2nd",
                  "4"
                ],
                [
                  "Auth",
                  "1st (first)",
                  "5, then the app"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CORS wraps auth==, so 401/403 responses still carry CORS headers",
                "Without that, the browser cannot read the error"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The 500 Gap",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "ServerError",
                    "sub": "outside all",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Your middleware",
                    "sub": "user stack",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ExceptionMiddleware",
                    "sub": "HTTPException",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Endpoint",
                    "sub": "raises"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Missing headers on 500",
              "text": "Unhandled 500s become responses in ==ServerErrorMiddleware==, outside your stack, so custom middleware headers are **missing** on them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Built-in Middleware: GZip and TrustedHost",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Built-in Middleware: GZip and TrustedHost",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. GZipMiddleware",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "app.add_middleware(",
                "    GZipMiddleware,",
                "    minimum_size=1000,",
                "    compresslevel=9)"
              ],
              "note": "minimum_size defaults to 500 bytes"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Accept-Encoding: gzip?",
                    "sub": "client asks",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Body >= minimum_size?",
                    "sub": "bytes",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Compress",
                    "sub": "Content-Encoding: gzip",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Adds ==Content-Encoding: gzip== and ==Vary: Accept-Encoding==",
                "Skips responses that are already encoded",
                "Streaming responses are compressed **chunk by chunk**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. TrustedHostMiddleware",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "app.add_middleware(",
                "    TrustedHostMiddleware,",
                "    allowed_hosts=['example.com',",
                "                   '*.example.com'])"
              ],
              "note": "checks the Host header"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Host not allowed",
                  "{red:400} `Invalid host header`"
                ],
                [
                  "`'*.example.com'`",
                  "Subdomains only, **not** the bare domain: list both"
                ],
                [
                  "`allowed_hosts=['*']`",
                  "Disables the check"
                ],
                [
                  "`www_redirect=True`",
                  "Bare host redirects if only its www form is listed"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Blocks ==Host header attacks==",
                "Too tight: health checks by **IP** or `localhost` break",
                "Do not compress small or already-compressed data (images, zips): wastes CPU"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Exceptions and Custom Handlers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Exceptions and Custom Handlers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Raise and Register",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`raise HTTPException` stops the endpoint and returns JSON `{\"detail\": ...}`",
                "==detail== can be any JSON-serializable value, not only a string",
                "`headers=` adds custom response headers",
                "Handler is chosen by the ==exception class== and its parents"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class MyError(Exception): ...",
                "@app.exception_handler(MyError)",
                "async def h(request, exc):",
                "    return JSONResponse(status_code=418, content={\"msg\": \"x\"})",
                "",
                "raise HTTPException(404, detail=\"Item not found\",",
                "                    headers={\"X-Error\": \"x\"})"
              ],
              "note": "custom handler, then a raise"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Override the Defaults",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Handle",
                "Catches"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`StarletteHTTPException`",
                  "your raises, unknown-route 404s, Starlette errors"
                ],
                [
                  "FastAPI `HTTPException`",
                  "only errors you raise"
                ],
                [
                  "`RequestValidationError`",
                  "bad body, query or path → ==422=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`exc.errors()` is a list of dicts: `loc`, `msg`, `type`",
                "Custom validation handler reads `exc.errors()` and `exc.body`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not in middleware",
              "text": "Middleware exceptions bypass the handlers. ==Return a JSONResponse== there; keep HTTPException for endpoints and dependencies."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why handle the Starlette class?** FastAPI's subclass misses unknown-route 404s",
                "**Which handler runs?** The nearest class match, walking up the parents"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Consistent Errors and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
